# Database

Scope: `implesia-mart-backend` only.

- Queries go through SQLAlchemy. Do not build SQL by concatenating request input.
- Production uses a database role that can change application data and cannot create roles or read other databases.
- Pool size stays bounded. Do not open a new connection per row.
- Columns used in filters and sorts keep an index. Foreign keys are real constraints, not comments.
- A write that updates more than one row, including stock plus an order line, runs in one transaction.
- Money and stock checks happen inside that transaction with a row lock or an atomic update, so two checkouts cannot both take the last unit. See `commerce-security.mdc`.
